From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 17:25:38 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 24/79] runner: the circuit loader, exact CPU evaluator and
 thread placement in core

First slice of the in-thinking runner port, from the DSV41
release branch (7b79ef92d) unchanged except for names:

- runner_api.zig: the runner's backend interface (programs, cells, results).
- runner_circuit*.zig: the TFIMR001 container loader, the exact CPU
  evaluator (incremental, memoised heads), the RV32 ELF boot and the circuit
  backend; golden and tiny-circuit tests.
- runner_place.zig: where runner threads run (a CPU set and niceness off the
  engine's), read under the binding's prefix; Linux-only syscalls compile out.

Build: test-runner-circuit-host (in test-cuda-host), bench-runner-circuit,
bench-runner-place. Nothing in the engine or server imports it yet. Comments
and the one log line name the generic <prefix>_CPUS / TF_RUNNER_* spelling.
